> What should I do next time this happens?? 

Conflict.  You didn't have it but you could have polypiled or wished.

I think free action would have helped too.

You had a wand of wishing (0:0) and a scroll of charging.  No holy 
water, oddly enough.

You should have, before leaving for the planes, blanked your junk 
potions and turned them into holy water, blessed the scroll, recharged 
the wand, used the four wishes to improve your AK...

>  I know, I had healing potions and an amulet of lifesaving in the 
bag,

You also had a scroll of taming and a ring of regeneration.

You had a couple unused ?EA, even if you weren't going to wish for a 
marker and write more.

> but the potions would have been destroyed in open inventory

It's worth the risk to carry one !FH openly.

You also had:

  a blessed potion of healing
  a blessed potion of speed
  a cursed potion of full healing
  3 uncursed potions of healing
  an uncursed potion of full healing
  2 uncursed potions of speed
  2 blessed potions of full healing
  3 uncursed potions of extra healing
  2 cursed potions of speed
  a blessed potion of extra healing

Which, when properly alchemised and blessed, would give you 71 more max 
HP, and still let you keep two !FH in reserve.  If you had saved a 
single !GL or !GE for the next alchemy step, that's 104 max HP instead, 
still with two !FH in reserve.

If you wished up a /poly and polypiled holy water before alchemizing, 
you could gain quite a lot of max HP indeed, limited only by the amount 
of holy water you could scrounge up by blanking junk potions.


> lifesaving won't do me much good when I have to sacrifice reflection
> to get it.

You could have worn a shield of reflection.

Or worn SDSM + cloak of magic resistance.



